# `x | f` pipes into a function, `f | g` composes two, as the sugar rules of lib/sugar/calls.warp (card pure-pipes)

# a value piped through functions of the program, left to right
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; y = 3 | inc | dbl; y' 8

# a pipe in an argument
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; print(4 | inc)' 5

# two functions piped together are their composition, a function value
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; both = inc | dbl; both(1)' 4

# a composition as an iteration's function
is! 'inc(x) := x + 1; dbl(x) := x * 2; [1, 2].map(inc | dbl)' [4 6]

# a value piped into a library word of one value
is! '" ab " | trim' 'ab'

# between values the bar stays the logical or
is! 'a = yes; b = no; a | b' yes
